-invoicing process; and managed services, including indirect tax return preparation, filing and tax payment, and notice management. The company sells its software products through software licenses and software as a service subscription. Vertex, Inc. has a strategic collaboration with xSuite Group GmbH to support SAP customers. The company was founded in 1978 and is headquartered in King of Prussia, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher David Young | CEO, President & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $615,917 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $356K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 15%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $28K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Vertex, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $2.8B market cap on $748M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -1% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 61% confirm genuine pricing power.","Accruals are elevated at -12.5% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.4%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 7.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 270% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.6956169094507345},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Large open-market insider purchases (net $1.3M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Vertex (VERX) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/vertex-verx-q3-2026-earnings-181352000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793903116.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What Vertex (VERX) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/vertex-verx-said-q3-earnings-091427345.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793870